# Line endings are pinned so a checkout reproduces what was committed.
#
# The verification reads the manuscript and refuses stray control characters,
# which is what catches a markup macro silently turned into the character its
# escape names. A carriage return is such a character. The committed blobs hold
# line feeds only, but git converts them on checkout wherever core.autocrlf is
# left at its Windows default, and the run then fails on a clean clone with one
# carriage return per line and nothing wrong with the repository.
#
# Pinning the working-tree ending here makes the checkout independent of whoever
# is checking out. Nothing is rewritten by this: the blobs are already line feed.

*.md        text eol=lf
*.cpp       text eol=lf
*.h         text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.tex       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
